KG42.register("clusters-501063f4ea2afdc4cf682c14",{"id":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v142-d-K001","paper":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets","label":"Prosumer voluntary participation, entry preparation and case resource boundary","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"Prosumer voluntary participation, entry preparation and case resource boundary","market_meaning":"Prosumers autonomously decide whether to participate and the conditions for providing flexibility, and before entry prepare a resource plan based on retail market costs and preferences. When they possess flexible generation resources, they may directly sell flexibility contracts; in the case, prosumers 46–55, who have no flexible resources, do not participate.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Voluntary participation and entry preparation belong to the general design; the lack of resources and non-participation of prosumers 46–55 belong only to the specified feeder case. Directly selling flexibility is not equivalent to obtaining permission to trade directly with the DSO; the latter is limited by the counterparty arrangement.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"Take the participation decision and entry preparation as independent functions, combined with the explicitly delimited case participation boundary. Counterparty permissions, contract allocation and payment are assembled separately; do not elevate case facts into general admission thresholds.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"The principal activity carrying voluntary participation, resource conditions and pre-entry planning."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"context","rationale":"Supplements the participation boundary of the specified case, retaining its resource-lack condition and participant numbers, and does not treat it as a necessary condition of the general participation rule."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31"],"rationale":"The general design states the autonomy of participation, while the case separately states that specific resource-less entities did not participate. The two supplement the scope of participation, but on this basis one cannot conclude that these entities actively refused to participate or infer a general resource admission regime."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G001","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The evidence in R001 supports case non-participation caused by lack of resources, whereas the existing definition of admission.local_area focuses on geographical eligibility; their conceptual scopes are not fully consistent.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::admission.local_area","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually confirm whether this node is allowed to carry such case resource conditions; if adjustment is needed, the upstream should revise the mapping separately. This round retains the original node and adopts only the narrowed case interpretation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G002","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B excerpts on which this cluster is based remain unverified and have only experimental candidate support status; the participation rule and case transcription have not passed independent source review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e34"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequent manual checking should verify the original text, case scope and node interpretation; in this round assembled only means that the candidate assembly within the limited scope is established."}]},"rule_refs":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R005","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R001"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-b249861ac893186a","KG31-5be8ae1142e7d54c"]});
